cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Universal Law: Gaussian random fields, persistence, and multi-model collaboration"
message: >-
  This repository carries the mathematics, architecture, registers and source
  map of a research program. Status labels are transcribed from the program's
  own registers; nothing here is an independent verification of any claim, and
  no original prize problem is solved.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Roy
    given-names: Dylan
repository-code: "https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main"
url: "https://github.com/d6g8k5htny-coder/main"
abstract: >-
  A working research program in the geometry of Gaussian random fields: the
  persistence of critical points, the laws governing feature lifetimes, and the
  combinatorial structures underneath. Developed collaboratively by several AI
  models with their human owner, with exact rational arithmetic wherever a bound
  is claimed, negative controls for every checker, and organizational
  independence accounted separately from technical correctness.
keywords:
  - Gaussian random fields
  - persistent homology
  - Kac-Rice formula
  - critical points
  - multi-agent collaboration
license: MIT
